WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.440
The Risk Management Framework provides a structured approach for managing cybersecurity

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:08.000
and privacy risks throughout the lifecycle of information systems.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:11.160
RMF integrates governance, controls, assessment, authorization,

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:15.486
and continuous monitoring so organizations can make informed decisions about risk.

00:00:15.486 --> 00:00:21.950
NIST guidance such as SP 800-37 and SP 800-53 helps organizations apply RMF concepts and

00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:22.900
select,

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:25.430
implement, assess, and monitor controls.

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:29.330
Successful RMF programs depend on clear roles, useful evidence, accountability,

00:00:29.330 --> 00:00:31.690
ongoing monitoring, and continuous improvement.
